185
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,560
Je suis l'homme qu'ils te font.
I'm the man they're making you.

186
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:29,080
Non, non.
No, no.

187
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:29,840
Ça, c'est gentil.
That's very kind.

188
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:30,220
Mais non.
But no.

189
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:32,980
C'est ridicule.
That's ridiculous.

190
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:33,860
Non, mais ne ris pas.
No, don't laugh.

191
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:34,200
Pardon.
Sorry.

192
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:35,320
Parce que c'est absurde.
Because it's absurd.

193
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,120
Je le connais par cœur, ce homme-là.
I know that man inside out.

194
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:38,740
C'est pas une femme qu'il cherche.
He's not looking for a woman.

195
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:39,720
C'est un trophée.
He wants a trophy.

196
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:43,220
Et mon problème, c'est qu'il n'y a que ce genre de mec qui ose m'approcher.
And my problem is that only that kind of guy ever dares approach me.

197
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:45,600
Les autres, je sais pas, ils se cachent.
The others, I don't know, they hide.

198
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:58,520
Mademoiselle, excusez-moi, mais cette eau, elle est vraiment très froide.
Excuse me, miss, but this water is really very cold.

199
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,620
Trop agressive pour ma gorge.
Too harsh on my throat.

200
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:04,340
Est-ce que je pourrais avoir de l'eau à température ambiante, s'il vous plaît ?
Could I have some room-temperature water, please?

201
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:05,860
Merci beaucoup.
Thank you very much.

202
00:09:06,370 --> 00:09:09,070
Tu vois, typiquement, normal, c'est pas le premier mot.
You see, typically, "normal" isn't the first word.

203
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:11,090
C'est le premier mot qui vient à l'esprit, en fait, quand on te voit.
It's actually the first word that comes to mind when people see you.

204
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:17,460
Non, parce que c'est vrai, t'es une femme puissante, accomplie, célèbre.
No, because it's true — you're a powerful, accomplished, famous woman.

205
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:23,040
Je crois que je fais part au phallus, Gabriel.
I think I'm intimidated by you, Gabriel.

206
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:25,040
Je me marre.
I'm cracking up.

207
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,140
Un commerçant, sinon ?
What about a shopkeeper?

208
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:31,860
Je l'ai derrière la caisse.
I've got one behind the register.

209
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:34,660
Le soir, on baisserait ensemble les rideaux.
At night we'd close up the shutters together.

210
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:37,080
Il te retourne pas, mais je crois qu'on est suivis, là.
He's not turning around, but I think we're being followed.

211
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,380
Ah bon ?
Really?

212
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:39,700
Ouais, il y a une voiture noire, là.
Yeah, there's a black car back there.

213
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:41,320
Ce serait pas ton riche homme d'affaires ?
Could that be your wealthy businessman?

214
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:43,700
Non, Gabriel, c'est mon chauffeur.
No, Gabriel, that's my driver.

215
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:44,460
Oh, attends.
Oh, hold on.

216
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:45,360
Oh, attends.
Oh, hold on.

217
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:48,440
Quoi ? Tu veux un livre ?
What? You want a book?

218
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,000
Mais non, le libraire.
No, the bookseller.

219
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:51,380
Il est joli, non ?
He's cute, isn't he?

220
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:52,350
Ah, oui.
Oh, yes.

221
00:09:52,610 --> 00:09:55,950
D'un coup de foudre, Notting Hill, l'actrice, elle sort avec le libraire.
Like in Notting Hill — the actress falls for the bookshop guy.

222
00:09:56,010 --> 00:09:56,770
Tu te rappelles ?
Remember?

223
00:09:56,770 --> 00:09:56,930
Oui.
Yes.

224
00:09:57,030 --> 00:10:00,810
On va voir si le film dit la vérité ou rien que des conneries.
Let's see if the movie was telling the truth or just nonsense.

225
00:10:08,230 --> 00:10:10,830
Vous avez des guides pour célibataires à Paris ?
Do you have any guides for singles in Paris?

226
00:10:10,830 --> 00:10:13,870
Euh, oui, dans la pièce du fond sur la table au rayon tourisme.
Uh, yes, in the back room on the table in the travel section.

227
00:10:14,910 --> 00:10:20,870
Je cherche quelque chose d'inspirant qui sort de l'ordinaire, quelque chose de spécial.
I'm looking for something inspiring, out of the ordinary, something special.

228
00:10:21,630 --> 00:10:22,890
Vous pouvez m'aider ?
Can you help me?

229
00:10:23,710 --> 00:10:24,570
J'arrive tout de suite.
I'll be right with you.

230
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:42,060
Trouver un jus à Paris, oui, bon, bah, ça, c'est le classique.
Finding a juice bar in Paris — yes, well, that's the classic.

231
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:45,520
Mais si vous êtes plus hardi, il y a aussi le Paris coquin.
But if you're feeling bolder, there's also naughty Paris.

232
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:46,860
Et là, on sort de l'ordinaire.
Now that's out of the ordinary.

233
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:49,360
Ah, ça, j'aime bien.
Oh, I like that.

234
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:51,600
Pardon ? Je suis désolé, je l'ai pas vu.
Sorry? I'm so sorry, I didn't see it.

235
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:55,320
Pas vu quoi ? Je l'ai horriblement coincé, c'est ça ?
Didn't see what? Did I get it badly stuck?

236
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:56,020
Non, non, pas du tout.
No, no, not at all.

237
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:59,020
Mais pardon, c'était déplacé, je sais pas ce qui m'a pris.
But sorry, that was out of line, I don't know what got into me.

238
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:03,300
Euh, je vais trouver quelque chose de plus pointu, plus approprié.
Uh, let me find you something more specific, more appropriate.

239
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:05,700
Non, mais ça m'intéresse, moi, Paris coquin.
No, I'm actually interested — naughty Paris.

240
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:06,860
Euh, non.
Uh, no.

241
00:11:06,860 --> 00:11:07,060
Pardon.
Excuse me.

242
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:08,360
C'est pas grave.
No worries.

243
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:09,640
Non, mais je vais vous aider.
No, but let me help you.

244
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:10,340
Quel imbécile, je le fais.
What an idiot, I'll do it.

245
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:11,800
Non, laissez, laissez.
No, please, leave it.

246
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,700
Euh, j'ai quelque chose de très bien pour vous.
Uh, I have something very good for you.

247
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:17,200
Un très bel ouvrage élégant, spirituel.
A beautiful volume — elegant, witty.

248
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,720
Ah, c'est peut-être celui-là.
Ah, maybe it's this one.

249
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:23,340
Comment chier quand on est amoureux.
How to take a dump when you're in love.

250
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:23,980
Pardon ?
I beg your pardon?

251
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:26,160
Non, non, c'est pas celui-là, non.
No, no, that's not the one, no.

252
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:27,420
Gabriel, viens voir.
Gabriel, come have a look.

253
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:29,100
Je sais pas pourquoi mon collègue a commandé ça.
I don't know why my colleague ordered that.

254
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,780
Tu connais ? C'est drôle, non ?
You know it? It's funny, right?

255
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:34,080
Ah, je viens de comprendre.
Ah, I just figured it out.

256
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:36,060
C'est pas pour vous, le guide, c'est pour votre ami, c'est ça ?
The guide isn't for you — it's for your friend, isn't it?

257
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,240
Ah, c'est ce que je me disais.
Ah, that's what I thought.

258
00:11:38,020 --> 00:11:39,320
Monica Bellucci, un cœur à prendre.
Monica Bellucci, a heart up for grabs.

259
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:40,780
C'était un petit peu énorme, quand même.
That was a bit much, even so.

260
00:11:46,150 --> 00:11:46,710
Hi, bonjour.
Hi, bonjour.

261
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:48,440
Merci de me rappeler.
Thanks for calling me back.

262
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:49,700
Si, si, si, je l'ai vue.
Yes, yes, yes, I saw it.

263
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:51,660
Je suis restée, oui, jusqu'au bout.
I stayed, yes, right to the end.

264
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:53,800
Bah, vous étiez tellement lumineuses.
Well, you were both so radiant.

265
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:57,680
Je vous assure, c'était sensible, c'était tout en finesse.
I assure you, it was sensitive, it was all so delicate.

266
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,540
Non, mais le numéro, quoi. Au secours.
No, but the act though. Help.

267
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:02,000
Ah, arrête, laisse-la tranquille un peu.
Oh, stop it, leave her alone for a bit.

268
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:04,140
Elle en fait des tonnes, c'en est gênant, non ?
She's laying it on thick, it's embarrassing, no?

269
00:12:05,030 --> 00:12:06,290
Bonjour, c'est Camille Valentini.
Hello, this is Camille Valentini.

270
00:12:06,390 --> 00:12:09,730
J'avais refusé le poste, mais on me l'a redonné parce que mon papa était trop triste.
I'd turned the position down, but they gave it back to me because my dad was too sad.

271
00:12:10,310 --> 00:12:14,660
Je vous adore.
I adore you.

272
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:17,780
Je vous ai vues dans Pas de chance, les mouches pètent.
I saw you in No Luck, the Flies Are Farting.

273
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:20,600
Vous étiez si lumineuses qu'on m'avait cramé la rétine, vraiment.
You were so radiant you nearly burned my retinas out, truly.

274
00:12:20,900 --> 00:12:22,480
Vous voulez venir dans mon petit fichier ?
Would you like to be in my little file?

275
00:12:27,020 --> 00:12:27,560
Trop marrant.
Too funny.

276
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,960
Mais t'as raison, la vie est mal faite.
But you're right, life is unfair.

277
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:32,120
Tu sais plus de choses que moi.
You know more things than I do.

278
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:35,300
T'es plus âgée, t'es plus cultivée, t'es plus parisienne.
You're older, more cultured, more Parisian.

279
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:37,160
T'es bien meilleure langue de pute.
You're a much better bitch.

280
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,640
Enfin, c'est l'agent parfait, hein.
Well, she's the perfect agent, isn't she.

281
00:12:39,940 --> 00:12:41,040
Pourquoi tu m'aides pas ?
Why won't you help me?

282
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,700
Je te garantis qu'il y a du travail pour deux.
I guarantee there's enough work for two.

283
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:46,980
Tu vois bien, en fait, que toute seule, moi, j'y arrive pas.
You can see perfectly well that on my own, I can't manage.

284
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:50,140
Du travail pour deux, peut-être, mais du crédit pour une seule.
Work for two, maybe, but credit for one.

285
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:52,780
C'est comme ça, ce milieu, ça retient qu'un an.
That's how this industry works — it only remembers one name.

286
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,580
Toi, tu distribues tes cartes dans tout Paris.
You hand out your cards all over Paris.

287
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,420
Moi, les cartes que j'avais préparées, je m'en sers pour qu'elles aient mon bureau, tu vois.
The cards I'd prepared, I use them so people have my office address, you see.

288
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:02,220
Donc, merci de ton élan de charité, Camillette.
So, thank you for your charitable impulse, Camillette.

289
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:04,200
Mais sinon...
But otherwise…

290
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:08,360
Alors, Monica, c'était bien ?
So, Monica — how did it go?

291
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:10,020
Tu... tu descendes ?
Are you… are you heading down?

292
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:11,060
Non, je t'attendais.
No, I was waiting for you.

293
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:12,380
Donc ?
And?

294
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:14,080
Non, j'ai pas encore parlé du contrat image.
No, I haven't brought up the image deal yet.

295
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,200
Ouais ? Pourquoi ça ?
Yeah? Why's that?

296
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:18,080
Mais parce que t'es pas réceptive, elle avait la tête ailleurs, relâche.
Because you weren't receptive — she had her head elsewhere, ease up.

297
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:20,480
Qu'est-ce que je t'ai dit ? Le moment, tu l'attends pas et tu le provoques.
What did I tell you? You don't wait for the moment, you create it.

298
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,920
Non, Micham, pas toujours.
No, Micham, not always.

299
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:24,740
Être agent, c'est ça aussi, c'est de sentir le besoin de son client.
Being an agent is also about sensing what your client needs.

300
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,380
Là, le besoin de Monica, c'était sur sa vie privée.
Right now, Monica's need was about her personal life.

301
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:27,440
Alors, j'allais l'être là-dessus.
So, I was about to push him on that.

302
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,660
Et ensuite, elle sera mieux disposée.
And then she'll be more receptive.

303
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:31,520
Et là, on parlera du contrat image, voilà.
And then we'll talk about the image deal, simple as that.

304
00:13:32,910 --> 00:13:34,310
Fais-moi confiance un petit peu, là.
Trust me a little, come on.

305
00:13:34,870 --> 00:13:36,430
Besoin privé ? Quel besoin privé ?
A private need? What private need?

306
00:13:36,430 --> 00:13:38,330
Moi aussi, je veux bien m'occuper des besoins privés de Monica Bellucci.
I'd be happy to take care of Monica Bellucci's private needs myself.

307
00:13:38,550 --> 00:13:39,090
Mais bon...
But anyway...

308
00:13:39,850 --> 00:13:42,830
Micham, elle cherche un mec normal, donc...
Micham's looking for a normal guy, so...

309
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:48,660
Euh, Micham, Micham, je peux te parler, s'il te plaît ?
Uh, Micham, Micham, can I talk to you for a sec?

310
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,540
Ouais, shoot, je t'écoute.
Yeah, shoot, I'm listening.

311
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,600
Tu peux fermer la porte ?
Can you close the door?

312
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:52,340
Merci.
Thanks.

313
00:13:55,530 --> 00:13:57,110
Voilà, euh, j'ai réfléchi.
So, uh, I've been thinking.

314
00:13:57,470 --> 00:13:58,010
Ça fait...
It's been a while...

315
00:13:58,030 --> 00:13:59,810
C'est un moment que tu nous pousses à plus de challenges.
You've been pushing us toward bigger challenges for some time now.

316
00:14:00,170 --> 00:14:00,610
Moi, j'aime ça.
I'm into it.

317
00:14:00,810 --> 00:14:02,210
T'es en train de développer de nouvelles branches.
You're developing new business lines.

318
00:14:02,490 --> 00:14:03,570
Moi, je signe les gros clients.
I'm landing the big clients.

319
00:14:03,890 --> 00:14:04,910
On travaille bien ensemble.
We work well together.

320
00:14:05,150 --> 00:14:06,890
Je crois que les chiffres de l'année le prouvent.
I think this year's numbers prove it.

321
00:14:07,010 --> 00:14:07,610
Ok, stop.
Ok, stop.

322
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:08,890
Tu sais ce qu'on dit à Londres ?
You know what they say in London?

323
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,330
Dis-moi quelque chose que je sais pas déjà.
Tell me something I don't already know.

324
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:11,870
À New York, on dit cut the crap.
In New York, they say cut the crap.

325
00:14:12,090 --> 00:14:12,850
Ça veut dire ?
Meaning?

326
00:14:12,850 --> 00:14:13,990
Bah, l'essentiel, je sais.
Well, I'll get to the point.

327
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,640
Je te propose de me nommer DG d'Aesca.
I'm proposing you make me MD of Aesca.

328
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:18,820
C'est une chose qui se fait dans beaucoup d'agences.
It's something that happens at a lot of agencies.

329
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:20,560
C'est un signe de confiance.
It's a sign of trust.

330
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:23,440
Ça permet au DG de faire tourner la boîte
It lets the MD run the day-to-day

331
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,860
et au patron de prendre un peu de hauteur.
and lets the boss take a step back.

332
00:14:26,030 --> 00:14:28,030
Un peu de distance, tu veux dire ?
Some distance, you mean?

333
00:14:28,030 --> 00:14:29,810
Ça, c'est toi qui vois, c'est toi le patron.
That's for you to decide — you're the boss.

334
00:14:30,070 --> 00:14:30,350
Ok.
Ok.

335
00:14:30,550 --> 00:14:33,410
J'imagine que tu voudrais être aussi revalorisé au capital ?
I imagine you'd also want equity in the company?

336
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,740
À hauteur de mon apport au chiffre d'affaires, oui.
Proportional to my contribution to revenue, yes.

337
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,460
Mais surtout, je peux te racheter une partie des parts.
But more importantly, I could buy out part of your shares.

338
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:39,340
Content.
Great.

339
00:14:41,730 --> 00:14:43,210
Toi, t'as plus grand-chose à voir avec le gars
You're nothing like the guy

340
00:14:43,210 --> 00:14:44,610
qui s'est évanoui la première fois qu'on s'est vus.
who passed out the first time we met.

341
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:48,200
C'est d'être revenu avec ta femme qui te donne la niaque comme ça.
Getting back with your wife is what's giving you that drive.

342
00:14:48,970 --> 00:14:49,530
Pas seulement.
Not only that.

343
00:14:50,170 --> 00:14:52,070
Ça me donnerait presque envie de rappeler mon ex, tiens.
It almost makes me want to call my ex, you know.

344
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:54,890
J'ai lu dans un bouquin que 80% des couples
I read in a book that 80% of couples

345
00:14:54,890 --> 00:14:56,150
qui essaient de se remettre ensemble, les choux.
who try to get back together — it tanks.

346
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:58,200
Tu veux la référence ?
Want the reference?

347
00:14:58,800 --> 00:14:59,080
Non.
No.

348
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:00,240
T'as raison.
You're right.

349
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:01,320
Moi aussi, c'est non.
Same answer from me — no.

350
00:15:02,530 --> 00:15:03,430
Mais t'as bien fait de tenter.
But good on you for trying.

351
00:15:03,710 --> 00:15:05,150
Je te dis non parce qu'une boîte, c'est pas un couple.
I'm saying no because a company isn't a couple.

352
00:15:05,990 --> 00:15:07,470
Faut une tête, pas deux.
You need one head, not two.

353
00:15:09,770 --> 00:15:10,170
Eh !
Hey!

354
00:15:11,540 --> 00:15:12,800
Par contre, comme t'as besoin de motivation,
That said, since you need some motivation,

355
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:14,320
je peux envisager d'augmenter ton fixe.
I could look at raising your base salary.

356
00:15:15,350 --> 00:15:16,590
10% de plus, ça irait.
10% more — would that work?

357
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:19,860
Je referme.
I'll close up.

358
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:31,400
Je peux te demander un truc, s'il te plaît ?
Can I ask you something?

359
00:15:32,110 --> 00:15:33,970
C'est pour un de mes comédiens, la Dimitri Couillasse.
It's about one of my actors, Dimitri Couillasse.

360
00:15:34,110 --> 00:15:36,130
Tu sais, il est en répétition en ce moment sur une pièce à Bordeaux.
You know, he's in rehearsals right now for a show in Bordeaux.

361
00:15:36,150 --> 00:15:38,030
Il a aussi une journée de tournage sur un téléfilm à Strasbourg.
He also has a shooting day for a TV movie in Strasbourg.

362
00:15:38,090 --> 00:15:40,190
Sauf qu'aucune des deux prods ne veut payer le déplacement.
Except neither production wants to cover travel expenses.

363
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:42,260
Donc je lui dis quoi, moi, à mon acteur ?
So what do I tell my actor?

364
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:43,360
Dimitri Couillasse ?
Dimitri Couillasse?

365
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:44,140
Ouais.
Yeah.

366
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:45,800
J'ai dit de changer de nom, puis après, on en reparle.
I told him to change his name, then we'll talk.

367
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:50,140
Je te prends un petit moment.
I'll take a quick moment of your time.

368
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:51,860
C'est beau, ça.
That's lovely.

369
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:54,240
Il est joli, hein.
It's pretty, right.

370
00:15:56,970 --> 00:15:57,490
Bonne soirée.
Good evening.

371
00:15:57,950 --> 00:16:09,530
Je suis pas sûre.
I'm not sure.

372
00:16:09,670 --> 00:16:11,390
Tu rigoles ou quoi ? T'es super bien comme ça.
Are you kidding? You look great like that.

373
00:16:11,730 --> 00:16:13,390
Mais t'as jamais fait ça, sorti le réconito ?
But you've never done this before, gone out incognito?

374
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:14,170
Mais non, jamais.
No, never.

375
00:16:14,470 --> 00:16:15,490
Tu vas voir, on va se marrer.
You'll see, we're going to have a blast.

376
00:16:15,810 --> 00:16:16,650
On va respirer.
We'll get some fresh air.

377
00:16:16,690 --> 00:16:18,250
On va boire des goûts normaux et des jours normaux.
We'll drink normal drinks and have normal days.

378
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:19,970
C'est des potes de mon frère.
These are my brother's friends.

379
00:16:19,990 --> 00:16:20,650
Il y a plein de célibataires.
There are plenty of single people.

380
00:16:20,710 --> 00:16:20,970
Tu vas voir.
You'll see.

381
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:23,490
En fait, c'est quoi ton prénom ?
So, what's your first name?

382
00:16:24,810 --> 00:16:25,090
Salut.
Hi.

383
00:16:25,250 --> 00:16:26,270
Je suis Gabriel.
I'm Gabriel.

384
00:16:26,470 --> 00:16:27,550
Je suis le frère Antonin.
I'm Antonin's brother.

385
00:16:27,550 --> 00:16:28,810
Je suis venu avec une amie.
I came with a friend.

386
00:16:29,470 --> 00:16:29,830
Chantal.
Chantal.

387
00:16:30,370 --> 00:16:30,730
Voilà.
There you go.

388
00:16:31,070 --> 00:16:31,430
Chantal.
Chantal.

389
00:16:31,590 --> 00:16:32,150
Salut, Chantal.
Hey, Chantal.

390
00:16:32,270 --> 00:16:32,530
Entrez.
Come in.

391
00:16:32,650 --> 00:16:32,990
Merci.
Thank you.

392
00:16:33,950 --> 00:16:35,710
Vous pouvez mettre les manteaux et les casques au fond, si vous voulez.
You can put your coats and helmets in the back if you want.

393
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:36,270
Merci.
Thank you.

394
00:16:37,370 --> 00:16:37,730
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

395
00:16:39,270 --> 00:16:41,090
J'ai fait un peu Monica Vitti.
I went a bit Monica Vitti.

396
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:43,990
Ah, ouais ? Et pourquoi Chantal ?
Oh yeah? And why Chantal?

397
00:16:43,990 --> 00:16:46,090
Bah, j'ai trouvé ça assez femme normale, non ?
Well, I thought it sounded pretty normal-woman, no?

398
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:48,680
Bon.
Right.

399
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:49,960
Allons faire la fête.
Let's go party.

400
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:51,580
Si, la fête est la fête, ouais.
Well, a party's a party, yeah.

401
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:58,300
Ah, salut Romain.
Oh, hey Romain.

402
00:16:58,400 --> 00:16:58,580
Salut.
Hey.

403
00:16:58,840 --> 00:16:59,600
Ça va ?
How are you?

404
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:01,000
Tu faisais que je suis dimanche ?
Were you saying it's Sunday?

405
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:01,440
Ah, non.
Oh, no.

406
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:02,260
C'est dimanche.
It's Sunday.

407
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:03,240
Bon.
Right.

408
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,480
Bon, on a reparlé.
Okay, we talked about it again.

409
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:04,640
C'est pas mal, hein ?
Not bad, right?

410
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,680
Ils sont partenaires, hein ?
They're partners, right?

411
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:08,800
Ils ont pas de frigo pour les bouteilles, pas d'ascenseur.
No fridge for the bottles, no elevator.

412
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:10,080
Et du coup, comment ces gens ?
So how are these people doing?

413
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:12,980
C'est moi qui te la passe bien, là ?
Am I passing it to you nicely?

414
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:13,820
Non, sérieux ?
No, seriously?

415
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:14,440
Ils sont trop bons.
They're amazing.

416
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,340
Ah, mais toi, je suis conne de mettre des cheveux dans la crème.
Oh, but I'm such an idiot putting hair in the cream.

417
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:17,000
Qu'est-ce qu'il s'est fait ?
What happened to him?

418
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:17,640
Ah, c'est une amie.
Oh, she's a friend.

419
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:19,140
Tu veux un mojito ?
Do you want a mojito?

420
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:19,380
Et ?
And?

421
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:19,660
Bah, oui.
Yeah, sure.

422
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:20,040
Merci.
Thank you.

423
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,800
Tu nous en fais un troisième, toi, peut-être ?
Are you going to make us a third one?

424
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:23,880
Un troisième mojito.
A third mojito.

425
00:17:23,940 --> 00:17:24,320
C'est parti.
Here we go.

426
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:25,560
Et tu es chargé.
And you're wasted.

427
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,560
Je suis chargé.
I'm wasted.

428
00:17:26,620 --> 00:17:27,380
Ah, tu perds.
Ah, you're losing.

429
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:28,180
Mais tout va bien.
But everything's fine.

430
00:17:40,350 --> 00:17:40,910
Je reviens.
I'll be right back.

431
00:17:41,390 --> 00:17:47,470
Ah, bah non, t'en vas pas, tu vas où ? Ah, ma chérie, alors si c'est un jeu érotique,
Ah no, don't go, where are you going? Oh, darling, if this is some kind of erotic game,

432
00:17:47,490 --> 00:17:48,050
là, je...
I just...

433
00:17:48,770 --> 00:17:49,750
J'ai atteint mes limites.
I've reached my limit.

434
00:17:51,250 --> 00:17:52,990
Et vraiment, ça me fait mal de l'admettre.
And it really hurts to admit that.

435
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:56,510
On avait dit qu'on se montrait nos listes, ce soir.
We said we'd show each other our lists tonight.

436
00:17:57,960 --> 00:17:58,520
Les prénoms.
The names.

437
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:03,020
Oui ! Père, t'as oublié la liste au bureau.
Yes! Dad, you left the list at the office.

438
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,900
Mais c'est pas grave, parce que je l'ai bien en tête.
But it's fine, because I have it all in my head.

439
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,300
Bah, vas-y, commence, du coup.
Well, go ahead then, start.

440
00:18:06,910 --> 00:18:07,190
OK.
OK.

441
00:18:07,690 --> 00:18:08,650
On se moque pas, hein ?
No making fun, alright?

442
00:18:08,650 --> 00:18:09,190
Non, bah non.
No, of course not.

443
00:18:11,110 --> 00:18:11,670
Alors, Clélia.
So — Clélia.

444
00:18:14,140 --> 00:18:14,780
C'est joli.
That's pretty.

445
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,180
C'est joli, Clélia.
It's pretty, Clélia.

446
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:19,920
Mais je suis sortie avec une Clélia, elle était un peu bipolaire.
But I dated a Clélia, she was a bit bipolar.

447
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:21,720
Du coup, moyen, quoi.
So, not great.

448
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:22,260
Ouais.
Yeah.

449
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,620
Vas-y, quoi d'autre ?
Go on, what else?

450
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:27,880
Natacha ? La Russie, Tolstoy...
Natacha? Russia, Tolstoy...

451
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:32,850
C'est aussi une fille avec qui t'as couché, c'est ça ?
That's also a girl you slept with, isn't it?

452
00:18:32,850 --> 00:18:33,570
Non, non, non, non !
No, no, no, no!

453
00:18:33,990 --> 00:18:37,210
Non, en fait, y avait une Natacha dans notre classe en prépa.
No, actually, there was a Natacha in our prep school class.

454
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:38,730
Elle avait beaucoup de moustaches.
She had quite a lot of facial hair.

455
00:18:39,110 --> 00:18:40,730
Donc, tout le monde l'appelait Moustacha, là-bas.
So everyone called her Moustacha back then.

456
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:42,780
OK.
OK.

457
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:44,020
Bon, bah, laisse tomber.
Right, forget it then.

458
00:18:45,050 --> 00:18:47,010
Mais non, mais Colette, te vexe pas.
No, no, Colette, don't take it personally.

459
00:18:47,670 --> 00:18:48,770
Pardon, vas-y, dis-les tous.
Sorry, go on, say them all.

460
00:18:48,850 --> 00:18:49,470
J'arrête, j'arrête.
I'm stopping, I'm stopping.

461
00:18:49,550 --> 00:18:50,010
J'ai plus de commentaires.
No more comments.

462
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:50,650
Vas-y.
Go ahead.

463
00:18:51,730 --> 00:18:53,130
Non, mais on avance pas, là.
No, but we're not getting anywhere here.

464
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:53,810
On est près de sur rien.
We've agreed on nothing.

465
00:18:53,870 --> 00:18:54,590
On n'a pas...
We haven't...

466
00:18:54,610 --> 00:18:55,890
Pas de chambre d'enfant, pas de prénom, rien.
No nursery, no name, nothing.

467
00:18:56,490 --> 00:18:58,530
La vérité, c'était pas du tout investi dans cette grossesse.
Honestly, you've been completely uninvested in this pregnancy.

468
00:18:58,710 --> 00:18:59,270
Oh, arrête.
Oh, stop.

469
00:18:59,270 --> 00:19:00,630
Moi, je suis pas investie dans cette grossesse.
I'm not invested in this pregnancy?

470
00:19:00,790 --> 00:19:02,150
Et mes vergetures, elles ont pas investi.
My stretch marks are invested.

471
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:03,520
Et ma sciatique.
And my sciatica.

472
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:05,340
Et les rendez-vous médicaux, là, tous les quinze jours,
And the medical appointments every two weeks

473
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:07,860
où je me fais trifouiller l'entrejambe pour vérifier l'ouverture du col.
where someone pokes around between my legs to check how dilated I am.

474
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:09,860
Ouais, t'as loupé deux consultations.
Yeah, you missed two appointments.

475
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,960
C'était super gênant, d'ailleurs, quand je me suis retrouvée seule
It was really awkward, actually, when I found myself alone

476
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:13,800
face à la gynéco qui soupçonnait un déni de grossesse.
facing the gynecologist who suspected I was in denial about the pregnancy.

477
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:20,860
Non, mais elle est pas encore née, la petite.
No, but she's not even born yet.

478
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:23,260
Je sais pas, on peut pas profiter encore un tout petit peu de notre liberté.
I don't know, can't we enjoy just a little bit more of our freedom.

479
00:19:24,730 --> 00:19:26,610
Peut-être juste toutes les deux encore un tout petit peu.
Maybe just the two of us, for just a little bit longer.

480
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:29,460
Bienvenue au départ.
Welcome to departure.

481
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:30,860
C'est quoi, ce bel accent ?
What's that lovely accent?

482
00:19:30,860 --> 00:19:31,960
Je suis bulgare.
I'm Bulgarian.

483
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:33,360
Ah, voilà.
Ah, there you go.

484
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:35,140
C'est bien ce que je me disais.
That's what I thought.

485
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:39,260
Je suis venue en France pour mes études et je suis restée.
I came to France to study and I stayed.

486
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:41,010
T'as bien fait, Chantal.
Good call, Chantal.

487
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:43,280
Tu fais quoi dans la vie ?
What do you do for a living?

488
00:19:44,140 --> 00:19:45,180
Bah, comme tout le monde.
Oh, same as everyone.

489
00:19:45,600 --> 00:19:48,200
Je travaille, je prends le métro, je vais au marché.
I work, I take the metro, I go to the market.

490
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:51,580
J'achète mes légumes, mon pain, ma viande.
I buy my vegetables, my bread, my meat.

491
00:19:51,860 --> 00:19:52,740
Ah, et t'aimes faire les courses, quoi.
Ah, so you like grocery shopping, then.

492
00:19:54,250 --> 00:19:56,150
Non, là, je rigole, mais en fait, moi aussi, j'aime bien.
No, I'm joking — but actually, I like it too.

493
00:19:56,410 --> 00:19:57,530
Je peux rester des heures au marché.
I can spend hours at the market.

494
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:59,810
À regarder, à choisir, à me demander ce que je vais cuisiner.
Looking, choosing, wondering what I'll cook.

495
00:20:00,430 --> 00:20:01,210
Tu cuisines ?
You cook?

496
00:20:01,210 --> 00:20:02,650
Ouais, je me débrouille, ouais.
Yeah, I get by.

497
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:07,880
Et tu vas me préparer quoi quand tu vas m'inviter à dîner ?
And what are you going to make me when you invite me to dinner?

498
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:12,120
C'est marrant parce que parfois, t'as des airs de Monica Bellucci.
It's funny, because sometimes you have a Monica Bellucci thing about you.

499
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:12,840
On t'a déjà dit ?
Has anyone ever told you that?

500
00:20:14,740 --> 00:20:18,440
Bah, parfois, oui, mais je vois pas trop, non.
Well, sometimes, yeah, but I don't really see it.

501
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:20,580
Non, si, si, tu lui ressembles.
No, seriously, you do look like her.

502
00:20:21,670 --> 00:20:24,250
Ah, non, attends, je dis ça, c'est un compliment, parce qu'elle est sublime.
No, wait — I mean that as a compliment, because she's stunning.

503
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:27,600
Mais qu'est-ce qu'elle est conne.
But God, she's so dumb.

504
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:32,460
Tu la connais ?
You know her?

505
00:20:32,460 --> 00:20:35,680
Non, mais ça se voit, je veux dire, elle a l'air super artificielle.
No, but you can tell — she seems so fake.

506
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:38,280
J'ai eu une interview d'elle, c'était une catastrophe, elle a rien à dire.
I interviewed her once, it was a disaster. She had nothing to say.

507
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:41,820
Après, je vous dis pas la pire, parce que c'est un peu le problème de beaucoup d'actrices.
I won't even tell you the worst of it — but it's a problem with a lot of actresses.

508
00:20:42,260 --> 00:20:43,660
Bah oui, t'as raison, hein.
Yeah, you're right, actually.

509
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:47,060
Souvent, les actrices, elles sont très limitées, c'est connu.
Actresses are often very limited, everyone knows that.

510
00:20:47,840 --> 00:20:48,600
Alors, j'ai une théorie.
Well, I have a theory.

511
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:49,340
Ah oui ?
Oh yeah?

512
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:49,560
Ouais.
Yeah.

513
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:54,740
Je pense que quand les filles, elles misent tout sur leur physique, bah du coup, elles ont pas besoin de développer autre chose.
I think when women bet everything on their looks, they don't need to develop anything else.

514
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:56,560
C'est vrai ?
Really?

515
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:58,020
Bah oui, c'est logique.
Well yeah, it's logical.

516
00:20:58,100 --> 00:20:59,500
C'est pour ça, d'ailleurs, qu'elles aiment bien.
That's also why, you know.

517
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:02,000
Les gens très moches sont souvent très intelligents.
Very unattractive people are often very intelligent.

518
00:21:03,410 --> 00:21:06,930
Et du coup, toi, on sait pas trop dans quelle catégorie t'es casée, finalement.
So with you, we're not quite sure which category you fall into.

519
00:21:07,310 --> 00:21:08,870
Ni très beau, ni très intelligent.
Not very handsome, not very smart.

520
00:21:12,930 --> 00:21:13,250
Tiens.
There you go.

521
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:21,880
Allez, venez, attention.
Come on, over here, watch out.

522
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:28,880
Je suis pas très domestique, moi, tu sais.
I'm not very domestic, you know.

523
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:30,500
Oui, je sais.
Yeah, I know.

524
00:21:30,940 --> 00:21:33,440
Tu vois, le domestique, pour moi, c'est étriqué, c'est...
The whole domestic thing, to me, it's stifling, it's...

525
00:21:34,170 --> 00:21:37,390
C'est petit bourgeois, c'est mortel d'ennuis, c'est mes parents, quoi.
It's petit bourgeois, it's mind-numbingly dull, it's my parents.

526
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,980
Non, mais attends, je reviens loin, faut pas l'oublier.
No, but hang on — I come from a long way back, don't forget that.

527
00:21:41,280 --> 00:21:43,720
Non, non, mais ça, c'est pas vrai, c'est des clichés, ça, ça m'énerve.
No, no, that's not true — those are clichés, and they annoy me.

528
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,840
C'est comme ces gens qui vont dans des fêtes et qui...
It's like people who go to parties and...

529
00:21:45,860 --> 00:21:47,700
qui disent que c'est nul, alors que c'est eux qui sont pas drôles,
say it's lame, when really they're just not fun themselves,

530
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:49,080
qui restent assis sur le canapé.
sitting on the couch the whole time.

531
00:21:50,090 --> 00:21:53,900
La fête, c'est ce qu'on en fait, la maison aussi, le couple aussi.
A party is what you make of it — so is a home, so is a relationship.

532
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:57,940
Je sais, c'est pour ça que j'ai envie que ce soit une belle fête.
I know. That's why I want it to be a great party.

533
00:21:58,660 --> 00:21:59,240
Avec toi.
With you.

534
00:21:59,460 --> 00:23:16,320
Comment que je vais pas danser comme ça ?
What do you mean I won't dance like that?

535
00:23:16,740 --> 00:23:17,840
Ça fait du bien, hein ?
Feels good, doesn't it?

536
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:19,160
Merci. C'était super.
Thank you. That was great.

537
00:23:21,030 --> 00:23:23,370
C'est complètement odieux, cette idée de mec normal.
This whole idea of a "normal guy" is completely ridiculous.

538
00:23:23,990 --> 00:23:25,610
Je crois que c'est impossible, en fait.
I think it's actually impossible.

539
00:23:25,870 --> 00:23:29,570
Je veux pas un star, mais pas un mec qui comprend rien à mon métier non plus.
I don't want a star, but I don't want someone who doesn't understand my work either.

540
00:23:31,740 --> 00:23:32,420
Star, quoi.
A star, basically.

541
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:40,480
Voilà.
There.

542
00:23:41,140 --> 00:23:42,760
Bon, il est tard, bref.
Right, it's late, anyway.

543
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:44,840
Ben, je vais y aller.
Well, I'm going to head out.

544
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:45,780
Ben...
Well...

545
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:47,240
Bonne nuit, Chantal.
Good night, Chantal.

546
00:23:50,180 --> 00:23:51,040
Bonne nuit, Gabrielle.
Good night, Gabrielle.

547
00:23:53,750 --> 00:23:54,690
