920
00:46:00,560 --> 00:46:04,420
Tu t'es monté la tête tout seul, donc arrête de me faire culpabiliser à chaque fois qu'on se voit.
You worked yourself up all on your own, so stop making me feel guilty every time we see each other.

921
00:46:05,280 --> 00:46:05,560
Ok.
Okay.

922
00:46:06,650 --> 00:46:08,170
Et estime-toi heureux que je lui ai rien dit.
And count yourself lucky I didn't say anything to him.

923
00:46:13,240 --> 00:46:15,460
Et je te remercie de n'avoir rien dit à Julien, vraiment.
And I do thank you for not saying anything to Julien, really.

924
00:46:16,720 --> 00:46:17,700
C'est pas moi de le faire.
It's not my place.

925
00:46:18,180 --> 00:46:20,640
C'est très chelou.
It's really weird.

926
00:46:21,820 --> 00:46:23,260
C'est vraiment la moitié du film.
It's genuinely half the film.

927
00:46:23,820 --> 00:46:25,040
C'est pas mal que t'aies pas tout compris.
It's fine that you didn't catch everything.

928
00:46:25,820 --> 00:46:27,140
Je suis crevée.
I'm exhausted.

929
00:46:27,800 --> 00:46:30,720
Non mais sérieux, j'arrive pas à savoir si c'est une gousse ou du génie.
No but seriously, I can't tell if it's clueless or genius.

930
00:46:31,400 --> 00:46:32,180
Ce qu'on va lui dire.
What we're going to tell him.

931
00:46:33,040 --> 00:46:35,060
Ah bah t'as qu'à dire, c'est très singulier.
Well, just say it's very singular.

932
00:46:35,600 --> 00:46:37,040
C'est très courageux, ça marche toujours.
It's very brave — that always works.

933
00:46:37,600 --> 00:46:52,140
C'est marrant.
That's funny.

934
00:46:52,160 --> 00:46:53,780
C'est quoi ce buffet ? C'est tout végétarien ?
What is this buffet? Is it all vegetarian?

935
00:46:53,780 --> 00:46:54,940
Ouais, on dirait, ouais.
Yeah, looks like it, yeah.

936
00:46:55,440 --> 00:46:56,780
C'est quoi ça ? C'est aux concombres ?
What's this one? Is it cucumber?

937
00:46:56,780 --> 00:46:59,040
Vous avez rien à boire, là ? Vous cherchez quelque chose ?
Don't you have anything to drink? Are you looking for something?

938
00:46:59,040 --> 00:46:59,440
Très bien.
Very good.

939
00:47:04,010 --> 00:47:04,950
Merci, c'est gentil.
Thank you, that's kind.

940
00:47:06,370 --> 00:47:09,050
Pour moi, votre film, c'est comme un long clip.
For me, your film is like a long music video.

941
00:47:09,710 --> 00:47:10,030
Merci.
Thank you.

942
00:47:11,390 --> 00:47:12,830
Je vous souhaite le meilleur.
I wish you all the best.

943
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:20,410
Ok, les amis, il va falloir me dire très sincèrement ce que vous avez pensé d'un film.
Okay, friends, I need you to tell me very honestly what you thought of the film.

944
00:47:20,650 --> 00:47:23,690
Et on emploie pas les mots « singulier », « courageux ».
And we are not using the words "singular" or "brave."

945
00:47:23,690 --> 00:47:26,190
Ça fait dix personnes qui m'ont dit le même truc.
That's ten people who've told me the exact same thing.

946
00:47:26,290 --> 00:47:27,370
Moi j'en peux plus, je vais péter un câble.
I can't take it anymore, I'm going to lose it.

947
00:47:27,430 --> 00:47:27,770
Je vous le dis.
I'm telling you.

948
00:47:29,390 --> 00:47:31,730
C'est vrai qu'ils me disent que des banalités.
It's true, all anyone gives me is clichés.

949
00:47:32,030 --> 00:47:35,670
Alors que toi, t'as mis tout ton cœur dans ton travail,
When you've put your whole heart into your work,

950
00:47:35,910 --> 00:47:38,370
et y'a personne qui est foutu de me dire un truc précis.
and no one can be bothered to say anything specific.

951
00:47:39,070 --> 00:47:41,270
L'allégorie du buisson pubis, par exemple.
The allegory of the pubic bush, for example.

952
00:47:41,450 --> 00:47:42,650
Ça, vous, vous avez compris.
That — you understood that.

953
00:47:43,010 --> 00:47:45,370
Je sais pas, toi, mais moi, carrément, ouais.
I don't know about you, but me — absolutely, yeah.

954
00:47:45,550 --> 00:47:48,150
Ça, ça me rassure, parce que moi, je commençais à douter.
That's a relief, because I was starting to doubt myself.

955
00:47:48,690 --> 00:47:49,810
Faut pas !
Don't!

956
00:47:51,170 --> 00:47:51,570
Bravo.
Bravo.

957
00:47:51,570 --> 00:47:52,470
Merci, les amis, merci.
Thank you, friends, thank you.

958
00:47:52,710 --> 00:47:54,530
Le buisson pubis.
The pubic bush.

959
00:47:56,430 --> 00:47:56,830
Pardon.
Sorry.

960
00:47:57,790 --> 00:47:58,510
Bonsoir, Camille.
Good evening, Camille.

961
00:47:59,450 --> 00:48:00,090
Ah, bonsoir.
Ah, good evening.

962
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:02,320
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

963
00:48:03,400 --> 00:48:03,720
Euh...
Um...

964
00:48:04,590 --> 00:48:05,330
Ouais, j'ai...
Yeah, I...

965
00:48:05,330 --> 00:48:07,290
J'ai fait un peu ma timide hier soir.
I played it a little shy last night.

966
00:48:07,790 --> 00:48:08,430
Mais euh...
But, uh...

967
00:48:09,050 --> 00:48:11,170
Enfin, voilà, j'aimerais vraiment que tu me représentes.
Anyway, I'd really love for you to represent me.

968
00:48:11,650 --> 00:48:13,490
Ah, bah, merci, mais là, je...
Oh, well, thank you, but right now I...

969
00:48:13,490 --> 00:48:15,470
J'ai même parlé de toi à Vincent.
I even talked to Vincent about you.

970
00:48:15,750 --> 00:48:17,910
Tu sais, c'est celui qui jouait le roi Basile hier.
You know, the one who played King Basile last night.

971
00:48:18,110 --> 00:48:19,510
Parce que lui aussi, il veut changer d'agent.
Because he also wants to change agents.

972
00:48:19,590 --> 00:48:22,070
Donc, bah, je lui ai dit, il faut trop que tu rencontres Camille Valentini.
So I told him, you absolutely have to meet Camille Valentini.

973
00:48:22,150 --> 00:48:23,110
C'est le nouvel agent chez SK.
She's the new agent at SK.

974
00:48:23,550 --> 00:48:24,550
Non, non, vraiment, vraiment.
No, no, really, truly.

975
00:48:24,710 --> 00:48:26,910
Une fois, c'est quelqu'un d'hyper motivé.
She's someone incredibly driven.

976
00:48:26,990 --> 00:48:28,430
Enfin, d'un vieil agent, blasé.
As opposed to a jaded old agent.

977
00:48:28,870 --> 00:48:30,210
40 000 comédiens dans son fichier.
40,000 actors in her files.

978
00:48:30,410 --> 00:48:31,190
Enfin, tu vois.
You know what I mean.

979
00:48:31,750 --> 00:48:31,990
Salut.
Hey.

980
00:48:32,990 --> 00:48:33,230
Camille.
Camille.

981
00:48:33,350 --> 00:48:33,790
Ah, salut.
Oh, hi.

982
00:48:34,250 --> 00:48:34,990
Ah, bah, c'est marrant.
Oh, well, that's funny.

983
00:48:35,010 --> 00:48:36,050
Vous vous appelez tous les deux, Camille.
You're both named Camille.

984
00:48:42,300 --> 00:48:42,820
Ah, bah, je...
Oh, well, I...

985
00:48:42,820 --> 00:48:43,280
Je reviens.
I'll be right back.

986
00:48:45,010 --> 00:48:46,250
Je te jure, j'allais te le dire.
I swear, I was about to tell you.

987
00:48:46,310 --> 00:48:47,430
En plus, j'ai pas fait exprès.
Besides, I didn't do it on purpose.

988
00:48:47,450 --> 00:48:48,670
Ça m'est venu comme ça, si tu veux.
It just came to me, you know.

989
00:48:48,730 --> 00:48:49,370
Ça m'est tombé dessus.
It just fell on me.

990
00:48:49,830 --> 00:48:51,450
Ça t'est tombé dessus comme ça que tu prennes mon nom ?
It just "fell on you" that you'd take my name?

991
00:48:52,570 --> 00:48:54,310
Écoute, c'est toi qui est venue me demander de l'aide, aussi.
Look, you're the one who came to me for help, too.

992
00:48:55,010 --> 00:48:56,930
En 24 heures de prospection, je te ramène deux talons.
In 24 hours of prospecting, I bring you two leads.

993
00:48:56,990 --> 00:48:57,730
On regarde aussi le bon côté.
Let's look on the bright side too.

994
00:48:57,850 --> 00:48:58,870
Mais le bon côté de quoi ?
The bright side of what?

995
00:48:58,870 --> 00:49:00,290
On pourrait tous les deux être Camille Valentini.
We could both be Camille Valentini.

996
00:49:00,290 --> 00:49:01,210
On pourrait tout faire à deux.
We could do everything together.

997
00:49:01,430 --> 00:49:03,310
Se diviser le fichier, le boulot.
Split the files, the workload.

998
00:49:03,390 --> 00:49:04,470
Ce serait plus simple pour nous.
It'd be simpler for both of us.

999
00:49:04,710 --> 00:49:05,710
T'es un grand malade.
You're out of your mind.

1000
00:49:05,910 --> 00:49:17,210
Bon, je suis désolée, hein.
Well, I'm sorry, really.

1001
00:49:17,290 --> 00:49:19,190
Je vous ai un peu gâché votre soirée.
I've rather ruined your evening.

1002
00:49:19,490 --> 00:49:20,070
Non, non, oui.
No, no, it's fine.

1003
00:49:20,210 --> 00:49:20,650
Régalez.
Please, help yourselves.

1004
00:49:20,830 --> 00:49:21,930
Moi, je suis fondrée.
I'm exhausted.

1005
00:49:22,450 --> 00:49:29,660
Merci de m'avoir accompagnée.
Thank you for walking me in.

1006
00:49:30,300 --> 00:49:31,180
Je vais...
I'm going to...

1007
00:49:40,940 --> 00:49:41,640
Laissez-moi, vous.
Leave me alone, you.

1008
00:49:41,720 --> 00:49:42,140
Laissez-moi.
Leave me alone.

1009
00:49:42,160 --> 00:49:42,460
Laissez-moi.
Leave me alone.

1010
00:49:42,600 --> 00:49:42,660
Oui.
Yes.

1011
00:49:47,220 --> 00:49:47,660
Bon.
Right.

1012
00:49:54,650 --> 00:49:56,970
Je vous pose ça où ?
Where shall I put this?

1013
00:49:56,970 --> 00:49:57,670
Euh...
Uh...

1014
00:49:57,670 --> 00:49:58,610
Là, euh...
There, uh...

1015
00:49:58,610 --> 00:49:59,250
Sur la table.
On the table.

1016
00:49:59,630 --> 00:50:00,370
Mathias, merci.
Mathias, thank you.

1017
00:50:01,110 --> 00:50:05,910
C'est charmant, je vous...
That's very kind, I...

1018
00:50:06,360 --> 00:50:07,460
Bah, merci.
Well, thank you.

1019
00:50:07,980 --> 00:50:09,380
Je vous remercie.
Thank you very much.

1020
00:50:09,400 --> 00:50:12,100
Vous voulez qu'on vous prépare quelque chose à boire, à manger ?
Would you like us to get you something to drink or eat?

1021
00:50:12,100 --> 00:50:12,260
Euh...
Uh...

1022
00:50:12,260 --> 00:50:13,960
Vous savez, je peux faire des soupes avec rien, moi.
You know, I can make soup out of nothing, me.

1023
00:50:14,060 --> 00:50:14,800
Non, non, ça va.
No, no, it's fine.

1024
00:50:14,900 --> 00:50:15,500
Vous embêtez pas.
Don't bother.

1025
00:50:15,880 --> 00:50:16,240
Euh...
Uh...

1026
00:50:16,240 --> 00:50:16,780
Catherine, je...
Catherine, I...

1027
00:50:16,780 --> 00:50:17,500
On va y aller.
We should get going.

1028
00:50:17,540 --> 00:50:19,080
On va laisser Noémie se reposer, je pense.
We'll let Noémie rest, I think.

1029
00:50:19,180 --> 00:50:20,160
Vous êtes sûres ?
Are you sure?

1030
00:50:20,160 --> 00:50:20,860
Oui, oui, oui.
Yes, yes, yes.

1031
00:50:20,940 --> 00:50:22,240
Non, non, vraiment, euh...
No, no, really, uh...

1032
00:50:22,240 --> 00:50:22,560
Vous...
You...

1033
00:50:22,560 --> 00:50:23,260
Ça va.
I'm fine.

1034
00:50:23,700 --> 00:50:25,300
Je suis pas paralysée, non plus.
I'm not paralyzed, either.

1035
00:50:26,340 --> 00:50:26,700
Voilà.
There you go.

1036
00:50:26,860 --> 00:50:27,220
Bon.
Right.

1037
00:50:31,360 --> 00:50:31,720
Attendez.
Wait.

1038
00:50:31,720 --> 00:50:33,220
Pardon, mais il faut que ça sorte.
Sorry, but I have to say this.

1039
00:50:35,380 --> 00:50:38,200
Quand on était aux urgences, Mathias m'a tout raconté.
When we were at the ER, Mathias told me everything.

1040
00:50:41,120 --> 00:50:45,220
Et vous savez, Noémie, le désir inconscient, c'est ce qui nous gouverne.
And you know, Noémie, the unconscious desire — that's what drives us.

1041
00:50:45,720 --> 00:50:48,600
Et on dit même que la plupart des accidents sont des actes manqués.
They even say most accidents are Freudian slips.

1042
00:50:48,700 --> 00:50:50,680
Alors, moi, je vous pose la question.
So I have to ask you.

1043
00:50:50,840 --> 00:50:54,360
Est-ce qu'il y a pas une petite part de vous qui regrette, d'enfant ?
Isn't there a small part of you that has regrets — about a child?

1044
00:50:54,360 --> 00:51:00,890
Bah, quitter ASK pour un job à Boulogne ?
What, leaving ASK for a job in Boulogne?

1045
00:51:00,890 --> 00:51:01,210
Ah...
Ah...

1046
00:51:02,360 --> 00:51:03,140
Non, mais...
No, but...

1047
00:51:03,560 --> 00:51:07,720
En fait, comme je disais à Mathias, c'est un chasseur de têtes.
Actually, like I was telling Mathias, it's a headhunter.

1048
00:51:08,100 --> 00:51:09,400
Donc, je ne peux pas...
So I can't...

1049
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:10,720
Noémie est très compétente.
Noémie is very talented.

1050
00:51:10,860 --> 00:51:12,180
C'est normal qu'elle soit convoitée.
It's only natural she's being headhunted.

1051
00:51:12,480 --> 00:51:14,260
Non, mais on s'en fout des chasseurs de têtes.
No, but who cares about headhunters.

1052
00:51:14,580 --> 00:51:17,760
Moi, je sais que ça me regarde pas, mais enfin, c'est peut-être pas le moment, Noémie,
I know it's none of my business, but maybe this isn't the right time, Noémie,

1053
00:51:17,860 --> 00:51:18,220
non ?
is it?

1054
00:51:20,720 --> 00:51:21,220
Mathias ?
Mathias?

1055
00:51:23,680 --> 00:51:26,180
Bon, enfin, il est pas du tout doué pour dire ce genre de choses, mais...
Well, he's not great at saying this kind of thing, but...

1056
00:51:26,180 --> 00:51:29,020
Noémie, moi, je sais à quel point il tient à vous.
Noémie, I know how much you mean to him.

1057
00:51:41,670 --> 00:51:42,910
Je vais réfléchir.
I'll think about it.

1058
00:51:42,970 --> 00:51:43,690
De toute façon.
Either way.

1059
00:51:43,930 --> 00:51:44,250
Ah !
Oh!

1060
00:51:54,270 --> 00:51:54,770
Monika ?
Monika?

1061
00:51:54,770 --> 00:51:56,610
C'est Gabriel.
It's Gabriel.

1062
00:51:57,190 --> 00:52:05,610
Non, mais je suis en dessous de tout.
No, I am absolutely worthless.

1063
00:52:05,730 --> 00:52:08,880
Un quart des lâches.
A quarter of a coward.

1064
00:52:09,100 --> 00:52:11,900
Une espèce de raclure.
Some kind of scumbag.

1065
00:52:12,260 --> 00:52:12,580
Ça...
I...

1066
00:52:13,020 --> 00:52:13,940
Un détritus, voilà.
A piece of trash, that's what I am.

1067
00:52:14,240 --> 00:52:15,720
Bon, ça va, n'en fais pas trop, quand même.
Okay, that's enough, don't overdo it.

1068
00:52:16,700 --> 00:52:17,560
Non, mais c'est vrai, quoi.
No, but it's true.

1069
00:52:17,620 --> 00:52:19,280
Je suis vraiment la dernière des sous-merdes.
I really am the lowest of the low.

1070
00:52:19,380 --> 00:52:20,580
Non, mais arrête de te flageller.
No, stop beating yourself up.

1071
00:52:20,680 --> 00:52:21,580
C'est pénible, à la fin.
It's exhausting, honestly.

1072
00:52:23,400 --> 00:52:24,120
À moi, maintenant.
My turn now.

1073
00:52:24,780 --> 00:52:25,460
Quoi, toi ?
What, you?

1074
00:52:25,460 --> 00:52:26,700
Moi aussi, j'ai des trucs à dire.
I have things to say too.

1075
00:52:26,900 --> 00:52:27,420
Moi aussi.
Me too.

1076
00:52:27,500 --> 00:52:27,900
Moi aussi, j'ai honte.
I'm ashamed too.

1077
00:52:28,910 --> 00:52:30,730
Non, mais t'as pas vu le numéro que je t'ai fait ?
But did you see what I just pulled on you?

1078
00:52:30,730 --> 00:52:31,790
C'est moi qui suis pas bien.
I'm the one who's not okay.

1079
00:52:32,210 --> 00:52:33,150
Faire ça à son agent.
Doing that to your own agent.

1080
00:52:33,350 --> 00:52:35,910
Mettre en péril une relation de confiance de plusieurs années.
Putting a years-long relationship of trust at risk.

1081
00:52:35,990 --> 00:52:36,550
Pourquoi ?
Why?

1082
00:52:36,930 --> 00:52:38,950
Parce que je peux pas rester seule un petit peu ?
Because I can't be alone for even a little while?

1083
00:52:38,950 --> 00:52:40,190
Non, mais ça va pas, ma pauvre.
No, come on, you poor thing.

1084
00:52:40,350 --> 00:52:41,390
C'est normal, quoi.
It's normal, really.

1085
00:52:41,490 --> 00:52:42,190
C'est humain.
It's human.

1086
00:52:42,230 --> 00:52:43,770
C'est pénible, aussi, d'être seule.
Being alone is tough, too.

1087
00:52:44,370 --> 00:52:44,690
Oui.
Yeah.

1088
00:52:45,030 --> 00:52:45,450
Moi, je...
Me, I...

1089
00:52:45,450 --> 00:52:46,170
Ça me pèse, hein.
It weighs on me, you know.

1090
00:52:46,530 --> 00:52:47,730
Ça fait combien de temps, toi ?
How long has it been for you?

1091
00:52:50,850 --> 00:52:51,390
Trois semaines.
Three weeks.

1092
00:52:52,330 --> 00:52:53,750
Mais non, mais trois semaines, c'est rien.
No, but three weeks is nothing.

1093
00:52:53,830 --> 00:52:54,350
Trois semaines.
Three weeks.

1094
00:52:54,570 --> 00:52:54,730
Tu vois ?
See?

1095
00:52:54,730 --> 00:52:55,790
Tu vois, c'est ridicule.
See, it's ridiculous.

1096
00:52:55,910 --> 00:52:57,270
Je suis super nulle, un célibat.
I'm terrible at being single.

1097
00:52:57,350 --> 00:52:57,950
Je sais pas faire.
I don't know how to do it.

1098
00:52:57,950 --> 00:52:59,290
Je déteste ça.
I hate it.

1099
00:52:59,470 --> 00:53:00,250
Je tourne à rond.
I just go around in circles.

1100
00:53:00,330 --> 00:53:02,430
On dirait une mouche dans la lumière.
Like a moth around a light.

1101
00:53:02,650 --> 00:53:02,950
Non.
No.

1102
00:53:03,400 --> 00:53:04,700
On dirait pas une mouche, hein.
Not like a moth, come on.

1103
00:53:05,680 --> 00:53:07,280
Et toi, ça fait longtemps ?
What about you, has it been long?

1104
00:53:07,280 --> 00:53:07,900
Six mois.
Six months.

1105
00:53:08,220 --> 00:53:08,680
Oh, madonna.
Oh, Madonna.

1106
00:53:09,440 --> 00:53:12,100
Et encore avant, j'avais déjà accumulé pas mal d'expérience.
And even before that, I'd already racked up quite a bit of experience.

1107
00:53:12,800 --> 00:53:14,060
Je suis devenu assez bon, d'ailleurs.
I've actually gotten pretty good at it.

1108
00:53:14,720 --> 00:53:15,840
Mais j'ai appris un truc.
But I learned one thing.

1109
00:53:16,340 --> 00:53:20,680
Un truc assez imparable pour que le célibat soit heureux.
One pretty foolproof thing for being happy while single.

1110
00:53:20,820 --> 00:53:21,860
Et c'est quoi ?
And what's that?

1111
00:53:23,840 --> 00:53:24,440
L'amitié.
Friendship.

1112
00:53:30,340 --> 00:53:30,820
Excusez-moi.
Excuse me.

1113
00:53:30,920 --> 00:53:33,460
Je t'ai même pas proposé un café ou une infusion.
I didn't even offer you a coffee or a herbal tea.

1114
00:53:33,860 --> 00:53:35,000
Ah, je veux bien une infusion.
Oh, I'd love a herbal tea.

1115
00:53:36,850 --> 00:53:40,090
C'est juste qu'elle est chez là et elle est allée se coucher.
It's just that she lives here and she's gone to bed.

1116
00:53:40,770 --> 00:53:42,290
Et quand elle est pas là...
And when she's not here...

1117
00:53:48,030 --> 00:53:48,770
Alors ?
So?

1118
00:53:48,770 --> 00:53:49,730
Alors, bouilloire.
So, the kettle.

1119
00:53:50,660 --> 00:53:52,540
J'ouvre le couvercle avec le bouton.
I open the lid with the button.

1120
00:53:52,540 --> 00:53:53,200
Je mets de l'eau.
I add water.

1121
00:53:53,380 --> 00:53:54,620
Tu remplis jusqu'où ?
How far do you fill it?

1122
00:53:55,240 --> 00:53:55,640
Je...
I...

1123
00:53:56,250 --> 00:53:56,650
Voilà.
There.

1124
00:53:56,970 --> 00:53:58,390
Pour deux, à peu près 0,5.
For two, about 0.5.

1125
00:53:58,810 --> 00:54:00,890
Je pose sur le couvercle.
I set it on the base.

1126
00:54:00,930 --> 00:54:01,790
Je mets en route.
I switch it on.

1127
00:54:02,110 --> 00:54:02,830
Et l'infusion ?
And the tea?

1128
00:54:02,830 --> 00:54:03,930
Tu mets pas l'infusion dedans ?
You're not putting the tea in?

1129
00:54:03,930 --> 00:54:04,170
Non.
No.

1130
00:54:04,330 --> 00:54:06,030
Je mets l'infusion dans l'intérieur quand c'est chaud.
I put the tea inside when it's hot.

1131
00:54:06,890 --> 00:54:07,290
Capito.
Capito.

1132
00:54:08,410 --> 00:54:11,830
Et maintenant, tu vas me faire un tuto micro-ondes et un tuto four vapeur.
And now you're going to walk me through the microwave and the steam oven.

1133
00:54:12,850 --> 00:54:14,170
Là, c'est un peu plus compliqué.
That's a bit more complicated.

1134
00:54:14,570 --> 00:54:15,130
Chez là ?
Hello?

1135
00:54:16,030 --> 00:54:16,830
Chez là ?
Hello?

1136
00:54:18,110 --> 00:54:18,910
Chez là ?
Hello?

1137
00:54:19,450 --> 00:54:20,090
Help ?
Help?

1138
00:54:20,090 --> 00:54:49,690
C'est le ventre aussi.
It's the stomach too.

1139
00:54:49,930 --> 00:54:50,790
C'est n'importe quoi.
This is ridiculous.

1140
00:54:50,810 --> 00:54:51,310
C'est trop lourd.
It's too heavy.

1141
00:54:52,030 --> 00:54:52,910
Non, non, même pas.
No, no, not even close.

1142
00:54:54,060 --> 00:54:55,020
Non, non, c'est là, là.
No, no, it's right there.

1143
00:54:55,040 --> 00:54:56,240
C'est un bon gros bordel.
It's a complete mess.

1144
00:54:56,500 --> 00:54:58,340
Tiens, les yeux comme ça à 5 heures du mat.
Look at those eyes at 5 in the morning.

1145
00:54:58,360 --> 00:54:59,400
La tête en surchauffe.
Head's completely fried.

1146
00:54:59,520 --> 00:54:59,700
Oh.
Oh.

1147
00:55:01,290 --> 00:55:01,790
Oh, voilà.
Oh, there we go.

1148
00:55:01,890 --> 00:55:02,590
Je connais ça.
I know that feeling.

1149
00:55:03,090 --> 00:55:16,600
Je vous en ai.
I've got some for you.

1150
00:55:25,670 --> 00:55:26,450
C'est Hicham.
It's Hicham.

1151
00:55:26,590 --> 00:55:27,550
J'en peux plus, Gam.
I can't take it anymore, Gam.

1152
00:55:28,620 --> 00:55:29,380
J'en peux plus.
I can't take it anymore.

1153
00:55:30,630 --> 00:55:31,470
Moi, il m'étouffe.
He's suffocating me.

1154
00:55:31,490 --> 00:55:32,170
Toi, il t'écrase.
He's crushing you.

1155
00:55:32,210 --> 00:55:32,890
C'est plus possible.
It can't go on like this.

1156
00:55:33,070 --> 00:55:33,450
Je sais.
I know.

1157
00:55:33,610 --> 00:55:34,090
J'en peux plus.
I can't take it anymore.

1158
00:55:34,090 --> 00:55:34,410
J'en peux plus non plus.
Neither can I.

1159
00:55:37,990 --> 00:55:38,990
Oh non, moi aussi.
Oh no, same here.

1160
00:55:39,090 --> 00:55:40,190
Non, mais en même temps.
No, but at the same time.

1161
00:55:40,210 --> 00:55:40,990
Mais comment il fait ça ?
How does he even do that?

1162
00:55:43,780 --> 00:55:44,820
Si on se barrait ?
What if we left?

1163
00:55:46,540 --> 00:55:46,880
Quoi ?
What?

1164
00:55:47,300 --> 00:55:48,060
Où ça ?
Where to?

1165
00:55:48,060 --> 00:55:49,140
On prend tous nos talents.
We take all our talent.

1166
00:55:49,200 --> 00:55:50,080
On monte notre propre agence.
We start our own agency.

1167
00:55:50,420 --> 00:55:51,640
Non, non, c'est impossible.
No, no, that's impossible.

1168
00:55:52,400 --> 00:55:53,440
C'est trop risqué, en fait.
It's too risky, actually.

1169
00:55:53,660 --> 00:55:54,880
Gabriel, évidemment que c'est risqué.
Gabriel, obviously it's risky.

1170
00:55:54,900 --> 00:55:55,740
Mais enfin, on sera pas les premiers.
But come on, we wouldn't be the first.

1171
00:55:56,720 --> 00:55:58,560
Enfin, tu vois, ça fait partie de l'histoire de toutes les agences.
I mean, you know, it's part of the story of every agency.

1172
00:55:58,720 --> 00:55:59,920
T'imagines, là ?
Can you imagine?

1173
00:56:00,430 --> 00:56:02,010
Ça voudrait dire qu'on est nos propres patrons.
It would mean we're our own bosses.

1174
00:56:04,030 --> 00:56:06,590
Mais toi, là, Hicham, ça arrangerait rien du tout.
But Hicham, that wouldn't change anything for you.

1175
00:56:06,630 --> 00:56:07,430
Au contraire, non ?
On the contrary, wouldn't it?

1176
00:56:08,130 --> 00:56:10,350
De toute façon, il le sait qu'on peut plus bosser ensemble, maintenant.
Either way, he knows we can't work together anymore.

1177
00:56:11,290 --> 00:56:11,710
Carlette ?
Carlette?

1178
00:56:11,710 --> 00:56:12,130
Oui ?
Yes?

1179
00:56:12,130 --> 00:56:13,750
Et Mathias, qu'est-ce qu'on fait ? On le plante ?
And Mathias — what do we do, just ditch him?

1180
00:56:13,750 --> 00:56:14,650
Arlette, elle comprendra.
Arlette will understand.

1181
00:56:15,270 --> 00:56:15,710
Mathias, ça va.
Mathias will be fine.

1182
00:56:15,810 --> 00:56:17,570
C'est pas lui qui va nous donner les leçons de solidarité.
He's not the one to be giving us lessons in solidarity.

1183
00:56:18,170 --> 00:56:20,270
Qu'est-ce qu'on fait, les acteurs ?
What about the actors?

1184
00:56:20,270 --> 00:56:21,410
Ils nous suivraient, tu crois ?
You think they'd follow us?

1185
00:56:21,410 --> 00:56:21,870
Bien sûr.
Of course.

1186
00:56:22,110 --> 00:56:23,010
Je veux dire, y a aucune raison.
I mean, there's no reason they wouldn't.

1187
00:56:24,320 --> 00:56:24,800
Je sais pas.
I don't know.

1188
00:56:24,860 --> 00:56:25,520
Faut tâter le terrain.
We need to feel things out.

1189
00:56:25,900 --> 00:56:26,140
Faut...
We need to...

1190
00:56:26,140 --> 00:56:26,500
Ah non.
Oh no.

1191
00:56:26,760 --> 00:56:27,120
Surtout pas.
Absolutely not.

1192
00:56:27,160 --> 00:56:27,960
Faut pas tâter le terrain.
We don't feel things out.

1193
00:56:28,020 --> 00:56:28,740
Faut en parler à personne.
We don't tell anyone.

1194
00:56:28,860 --> 00:56:29,880
Parce que sinon, ça va fuiter.
Because otherwise it'll leak.

1195
00:56:29,920 --> 00:56:30,900
Et là, Hicham, il va se douter.
And then Hicham will get suspicious.

1196
00:56:31,560 --> 00:56:35,000
On fait quoi, alors ?
So what do we do?

1197
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:36,380
On fait toutes les démarches.
We handle all the groundwork.

1198
00:56:37,850 --> 00:56:40,250
Quand on est prêt, là, on en informe les acteurs.
When we're ready, then we tell the actors.

1199
00:56:49,730 --> 00:56:50,230
Là, on le fait.
Then we do it.

1200
00:56:50,230 --> 00:56:51,230
Sous-titrage MFP.
Subtitling by MFP.

1201
00:56:51,230 --> 00:56:51,470
»
»
